---
import ApplicationLayout from '../../layouts/ApplicationLayout.astro';

const jsonLd = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Product",
    "name": "DMB-062 Manual-Clean Centrifuge Module - Alfa Laval MAB 209",
    "description": "The Dolphin DMB-062 is a turnkey manual-clean purification module featuring a remanufactured Alfa Laval MAB 209 disc stack centrifuge, rebuilt, tested, and warrantied by Dolphin. Published diesel capacity at 40°C and 13 cSt is 14,100 L/h (62.08 US GPM, derived). Dolphin's largest manual-clean module for major turbine lube oil systems and high-volume industrial purification.",
    "brand": { "@type": "Brand", "name": "Alfa Laval" },
    "alternateName": "Alfa Laval MAB 209",
    "category": "Disc Stack Centrifuges",
    "model": "DMB-062",
    "offers": {
      "@type": "Offer",
      "availability": "https://schema.org/InStock",
      "priceCurrency": "USD",
      "seller": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "Dolphin Centrifuge" }
    }
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Article",
    "headline": "DMB-062 Manual-Clean Centrifuge Module (Alfa Laval MAB 209) - Specifications & Applications",
    "author": {
      "@type": "Person",
      "name": "Sanjay Prabhu MSME",
      "jobTitle": "Centrifuge Applications Engineer",
      "worksFor": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "Dolphin Centrifuge" }
    },
    "publisher": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "Dolphin Centrifuge" },
    "url": "https://dolphincentrifuge.com/centrifuges/dmb-062/"
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    "mainEntity": [
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What is the throughput of the DMB-062 centrifuge?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Published MAB 209 capacities are 14,100 L/h diesel fuel at 40°C and 13 cSt (62.08 US GPM, derived), 18,300 L/h gas oil at 40°C (80.57 US GPM, derived), 6,300–7,400 L/h R&O lube oil at 80–90°C (27.74–32.58 US GPM, derived), and 13,700 L/h steam turbine oil at 60–70°C (60.32 US GPM, derived). The rated reference is 21,000 L/h (92.46 US GPM, derived); its source fluid is unspecified."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What turbine or system size is the DMB-062 suited for?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "At the published R&O lube-oil range of 6,300–7,400 L/h at 80–90°C (27.74–32.58 US GPM, derived), the DMB-062 is suited for major power generation turbines above 30,000 HP, large marine turbine installations, multiple large turbines served by a centralized lube oil purification system, and large petrochemical compressor trains. It can handle oil reservoirs of 15,000–50,000+ gallons in continuous bypass operation."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What applications is the DMB-062 best suited for?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "The DMB-062 is Dolphin's largest manual-clean centrifuge, suited for major turbine lube oil systems (30,000+ HP), large marine engine lube systems, centralized lube oil purification for large industrial complexes, diesel polishing at 14,100 L/h at 40°C and 13 cSt (62.08 US GPM, derived), and gas-oil polishing at 18,300 L/h at 40°C (80.57 US GPM, derived)."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Why choose a manual-clean DMB-062 over a self-cleaning centrifuge at this size?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "For clean turbine lube oil applications where fluid cleanliness is high and solids loading is very low, a manual-clean unit like the DMB-062 often provides better economics than a self-cleaning unit. No hydraulic self-cleaning mechanism means lower capital cost, no self-clean control complexity, and simpler long-term maintenance. In large turbine systems, cleaning intervals of weeks or months make manual cleaning economically attractive."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How does the DMB-062 compare to the DMPX-070 self-cleaning model?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "The DMB-062 base machine has a published diesel capacity at 40°C and 13 cSt of 14,100 L/h (62.08 US GPM, derived). The DMPX-070 is a self-cleaning commercial class with more than one Alfa Laval base machine, so its capacity must be stated for the exact base machine and fluid. The DMB-062 is suited to low-solids feeds; the DMPX-070 is suited to significant solids or continuous unattended operation."
        }
      }
    ]
  }
];
---

<ApplicationLayout
  title="DMB-062 Manual-Clean Module - Alfa Laval MAB 209 | Dolphin Centrifuge"
  heroTitle="DMB-062 Manual-Clean Module - Alfa Laval MAB 209"
  disableTitleSuffix={true}
  description="Dolphin DMB-062 module with a remanufactured Alfa Laval MAB 209: published diesel capacity at 40°C and 13 cSt is 14,100 L/h (62.08 US GPM, derived)."
  canonicalUrl="https://dolphincentrifuge.com/centrifuges/dmb-062/"
  heroImage="/images/alfa-laval-mab-centrifuge/Alfa-Laval-MAB209-Biodiesel-Centrifuge.webp"
  heroImageAlt="Alfa Laval MAB 209 centrifuge reconditioned by Dolphin, supplied as the DMB-062 system"
  category="products"
  categoryLabel="Dolphin Manual-Clean Disc Centrifuges"
  toc={[
    { id: "specs", label: "Specifications" },
    { id: "capacity", label: "Capacity by Application" },
    { id: "applications", label: "Key Applications" },
    { id: "faq", label: "FAQ" },
  ]}
  relatedApplications={[
    { label: "Lube Oil Centrifuge", href: "/lube-oil-centrifuge/" },
    { label: "Fuel Oil Centrifuge", href: "/fuel-oil-centrifuge/" },
    { label: "Waste Oil Centrifuge", href: "/waste-oil-centrifuge/" },
  ]}
  relatedProducts={[
    { label: "DMB-037 Manual-Clean Centrifuge", href: "/centrifuges/dmb-037/" },
    { label: "DMB-019 Manual-Clean Centrifuge", href: "/centrifuges/dmb-019/" },
    { label: "DMPX-070 Self-Cleaning Centrifuge", href: "/centrifuges/dmpx-070/" },
  ]}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  hideBottomCTA={true}
>
  <article class="prose-dolphin max-w-none">

    <p>
      The DMB-062 is a Dolphin-engineered turnkey purification module featuring a remanufactured <a href="/alfa-laval-mab-centrifuge/">Alfa Laval MAB 209</a> manual-clean disc stack centrifuge, rebuilt, tested, and warrantied by Dolphin.
    </p>
    <p>
      Dolphin is the independent specialist in Alfa Laval centrifuges, backed by 40+ years of MAB rebuild and sizing experience.
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 italic">Dolphin is an independent remanufacturer and is not affiliated with or authorized by Alfa Laval.</p>

    <h2 id="specs">DMB-062 Specifications</h2>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-4">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Parameter</th>
            <th>Value</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Base machine</td><td>Alfa Laval MAB 209 (remanufactured)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Separation type</td><td>Two-phase clarifier (liquid-liquid or liquid-solid)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Diesel throughput at 40&deg;C and 13 cSt</td><td>14,100 L/h (62.08 US GPM, derived)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Rated reference (source fluid unspecified)</td><td>21,000 L/h (92.46 US GPM, derived)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Cleaning method</td><td>Manual (bowl disassembly required for solids removal)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Bowl construction</td><td>Carbon steel standard</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Power supply</td><td>460V / 3-phase / 60 Hz standard (other voltages available)</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 italic">Throughput figures are for typical fluids at listed conditions. Actual capacity varies with feed viscosity, temperature, density difference, and solids loading. Contact Dolphin Centrifuge for application-specific confirmation.</p>

    <div class="bg-gold/10 border-l-4 border-gold rounded-r-xl p-5 my-8 not-prose">
      <p class="font-bold text-navy text-base mb-1">Need the complete datasheet?</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-text-light leading-relaxed mb-4">We'll email the complete datasheet - usually within one business day.</p>
      <a href="/contact-for-alfa-laval-centrifuges/" class="inline-block bg-gold text-navy font-semibold px-5 py-2 rounded-lg hover:bg-gold/90 transition-colors text-sm">Request the full spec sheet (PDF) -></a>
    </div>

    <h2 id="capacity">DMB-062 Capacity by Application</h2>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Application / Fluid</th>
            <th>Published throughput (L/h and derived US GPM)</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Rated reference (source fluid unspecified)</td><td>21,000 L/h (92.46 US GPM, derived)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Gas oil at 40&deg;C</td><td>18,300 L/h (80.57 US GPM, derived)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Diesel fuel at 40&deg;C and 13 cSt</td><td>14,100 L/h (62.08 US GPM, derived)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>R&amp;O lube oil at 80&ndash;90&deg;C</td><td>6,300&ndash;7,400 L/h (27.74&ndash;32.58 US GPM, derived)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Detergent lube oil at 80&ndash;90&deg;C</td><td>5,300&ndash;6,300 L/h (23.34&ndash;27.74 US GPM, derived)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Trunk-piston detergent lube oil at 80&ndash;90&deg;C</td><td>3,800&ndash;4,600 L/h (16.73&ndash;20.25 US GPM, derived)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Engine lubricating oil at 80&ndash;90&deg;C</td><td>7,400 L/h (32.58 US GPM, derived)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Steam turbine oil at 60&ndash;70&deg;C</td><td>13,700 L/h (60.32 US GPM, derived)</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 italic">US GPM values are derived from the published L/h figures using 1 US GPM = 227.124707 L/h and rounded to two decimal places. See the <a href="/technical-data/#methodology">authoritative technical-data registry and methodology</a> for source basis and machine-readable records.</p>

    <h2>The Case for High-Capacity Manual-Clean</h2>
    <p>
      For applications with clean, low-solids fluid - such as turbine lube oil purification or clean diesel polishing - a manual-clean centrifuge at high throughput often provides better economics than a self-cleaning unit. Published diesel capacity at 40&deg;C and 13 cSt is 14,100 L/h (62.08 US GPM, derived), without the complexity, control system cost, and maintenance overhead of hydraulic self-cleaning mechanisms.
    </p>
    <p>
      In large turbine lube oil applications, fluid cleanliness is usually high (low particulate loading), and cleaning intervals are long - measured in weeks or months rather than days. A single DMB-062 on a planned cleaning schedule outperforms multiple smaller self-cleaning units from both cost and simplicity perspectives. Dolphin Centrifuge can help you calculate the optimal cleaning interval based on your fluid analysis.
    </p>

    <!-- Mid-Page CTA -->
    <div class="not-prose my-10 rounded-xl border-l-4 border-gold bg-gold/10 p-6 flex flex-col md:flex-row md:items-center gap-4">
      <div class="flex-1">
        <p class="text-navy font-bold text-lg mb-1">Specifying the DMB-062 for a major turbine installation?</p>
        <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">Our engineers can calculate your optimal cleaning interval, confirm sizing, and quote the right configuration for your power plant, marine, or industrial facility.</p>
      </div>
      <a href="/contact-for-alfa-laval-centrifuges/" class="shrink-0 inline-block bg-gold text-navy font-bold px-6 py-3 rounded-lg hover:bg-gold/90 transition-colors text-center">
        Request a Quote &rarr;
      </a>
    </div>

    <h2 id="applications">Key Applications</h2>
    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-10 not-prose">
      <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 border border-gray-200">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-navy mb-2">Major Power Generation Turbines</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Power station steam turbines and gas turbines above 30,000 HP with large lube oil reservoirs. Published MAB 209 throughput is 6,300–7,400 L/h (27.74–32.58 US GPM, derived) on R&amp;O lube oil at 80–90&deg;C and 13,700 L/h (60.32 US GPM, derived) on steam turbine oil at 60–70&deg;C.</p>
        <a href="/lube-oil-centrifuge/" class="text-sm font-semibold text-navy hover:text-gold transition-colors">Lube Oil Centrifuge Details &rarr;</a>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 border border-gray-200">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-navy mb-2">Bulk Diesel &amp; Gas Oil Polishing</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Large fuel depots, tank farms, and bulk storage terminals requiring high-throughput diesel and gas oil polishing. Published capacity is 14,100 L/h (62.08 US GPM, derived) on diesel at 40&deg;C and 13 cSt and 18,300 L/h (80.57 US GPM, derived) on gas oil at 40&deg;C.</p>
        <a href="/diesel-centrifuge/" class="text-sm font-semibold text-navy hover:text-gold transition-colors">Diesel Centrifuge Details &rarr;</a>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 border border-gray-200">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-navy mb-2">Large Marine Lube Oil Systems</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Large marine vessels with multiple propulsion turbines, main engine lube systems, and auxiliary machinery lube oil requiring centralized purification. The DMB-062 handles marine application conditions including variable pitch, shock loading, and the need for robust, reliable design.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 border border-gray-200">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-navy mb-2">Centralized Industrial Lube Systems</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Large industrial complexes, refineries, and chemical plants with centralized lubrication systems serving multiple large machines from a common reservoir. The DMB-062 handles the high throughput required for centralized purification of very large shared lube oil inventories.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- FAQ -->
    <h2 id="faq">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

    <details class="border-l-4 border-gold/40 pl-4 mb-4 not-prose">
      <summary class="font-semibold text-navy cursor-pointer py-2">What is the throughput of the DMB-062?</summary>
      <p class="mt-2 text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        Published MAB 209 capacities are 14,100 L/h diesel at 40&deg;C and 13 cSt (62.08 US GPM, derived), 18,300 L/h gas oil at 40&deg;C (80.57 US GPM, derived), 6,300&ndash;7,400 L/h R&amp;O lube oil at 80&ndash;90&deg;C (27.74&ndash;32.58 US GPM, derived), and 13,700 L/h steam turbine oil at 60&ndash;70&deg;C (60.32 US GPM, derived). The 21,000 L/h (92.46 US GPM, derived) rated reference has no source fluid specified.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details class="border-l-4 border-gold/40 pl-4 mb-4 not-prose">
      <summary class="font-semibold text-navy cursor-pointer py-2">What turbine or system size is the DMB-062 suited for?</summary>
      <p class="mt-2 text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        At the published R&amp;O lube-oil range of 6,300&ndash;7,400 L/h at 80&ndash;90&deg;C (27.74&ndash;32.58 US GPM, derived), the DMB-062 suits major turbines above 30,000 HP, large marine turbine installations, centralized <a href="/lube-oil-centrifuge/">lube oil</a> systems for multiple large turbines, and large petrochemical compressor trains with reservoirs of 15,000–50,000+ gallons.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details class="border-l-4 border-gold/40 pl-4 mb-4 not-prose">
      <summary class="font-semibold text-navy cursor-pointer py-2">What applications is the DMB-062 best suited for?</summary>
      <p class="mt-2 text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        Major turbine lube oil (30,000+ HP), bulk diesel and gas-oil polishing, large marine lube systems, centralized lube oil purification for large industrial complexes, and offshore facilities requiring maximum throughput in a manual-clean design. Published diesel capacity at 40&deg;C and 13 cSt is 14,100 L/h (62.08 US GPM, derived); gas-oil capacity at 40&deg;C is 18,300 L/h (80.57 US GPM, derived).
      </p>
    </details>

    <details class="border-l-4 border-gold/40 pl-4 mb-4 not-prose">
      <summary class="font-semibold text-navy cursor-pointer py-2">Why choose manual-clean DMB-062 over a self-cleaning centrifuge?</summary>
      <p class="mt-2 text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        For clean <a href="/lube-oil-centrifuge/">turbine lube oil</a> with very low solids loading, the DMB-062 provides lower capital cost, no self-cleaning control complexity, and simpler maintenance than a self-cleaning unit. In large turbine systems, cleaning intervals of weeks or months make manual cleaning economically attractive. <a href="/contact-for-alfa-laval-centrifuges/">Contact us</a> to calculate your specific cleaning interval.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details class="border-l-4 border-gold/40 pl-4 mb-4 not-prose">
      <summary class="font-semibold text-navy cursor-pointer py-2">How does the DMB-062 compare to the DMPX-070?</summary>
      <p class="mt-2 text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        The DMB-062 base machine has a published diesel capacity at 40&deg;C and 13 cSt of 14,100 L/h (62.08 US GPM, derived). The <a href="/centrifuges/dmpx-070/">DMPX-070</a> is a self-cleaning commercial class with more than one Alfa Laval base machine, so its capacity must be stated for the exact base machine and fluid. Choose self-cleaning for <a href="/waste-oil-centrifuge/">waste oil</a>, HFO, or crude oil processing where continuous automated desludging is essential.
      </p>
    </details>

    <h2>Related Resources</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/centrifuges/dmb-037/">DMB-037 Manual-Clean Centrifuge</a></li>
      <li><a href="/centrifuges/dmpx-070/">DMPX-070 Self-Cleaning Centrifuge</a></li>
      <li><a href="/disc-stack-centrifuge/">Disc Stack Centrifuge Overview</a></li>
      <li><a href="/lube-oil-centrifuge/">Lube Oil Centrifuge Applications</a></li>
      <li><a href="/contact-for-alfa-laval-centrifuges/">Contact Us for DMB-062 Pricing</a></li>
    </ul>

  </article>

  <!-- Bottom CTA Bar -->
  <div class="not-prose mt-12 rounded-xl bg-navy px-8 py-8 flex flex-col md:flex-row md:items-center gap-6">
    <div class="flex-1">
      <p class="text-white font-bold text-xl mb-1">Ready to specify the DMB-062?</p>
      <p class="text-white/80 text-sm">Call <a href="tel:+12485222573" class="text-gold font-semibold">(248) 522-2573</a> or email <a href="mailto:sales@dolphincentrifuge.com" class="text-gold font-semibold">sales@dolphincentrifuge.com</a> - 40+ years in centrifugal separation, Warren MI.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3 shrink-0">
      <a href="/contact-for-alfa-laval-centrifuges/" class="inline-block bg-gold text-navy font-bold px-6 py-3 rounded-lg hover:bg-gold/90 transition-colors text-center">Get a Quote</a>
      <a href="/industrial-centrifuge-sample-testing/" class="inline-block border border-white text-white font-bold px-6 py-3 rounded-lg hover:bg-white/10 transition-colors text-center">Sample Testing</a>
    </div>
  </div>

</ApplicationLayout>
